(ABSTRACT:) Tj
0 -15 Td
/F1 9 Tf
(Luira Phanit \(the Seed Sowing Festival\) is the supreme cultural and) Tj
0 -13 Td
/F1 9 Tf
(agricultural festival of the Tangkhul Naga people, celebrated annually) Tj
0 -13 Td
/F1 9 Tf
(in February across all traditional villages. This paper provides an) Tj
0 -13 Td
/F1 9 Tf
(ethnolinguistic documentation of the ceremonial liturgy performed during) Tj
0 -13 Td
/F1 9 Tf
(Luira. We record and translate the sacred Chithar \(first seed-sowing) Tj
0 -13 Td
/F1 9 Tf
(invocation\) chanted exclusively by the village chief \(Awungshi\), the) Tj
0 -13 Td
/F1 9 Tf
(liturgical formulas for domestic hearth renewal, and the poetic lyrics) Tj
0 -13 Td
/F1 9 Tf
(of the Hao Pheichak \(traditional circle dance\). The texts preserve) Tj
0 -13 Td
/F1 9 Tf
(archaic lexical roots unrecorded in modern dictionaries.) Tj
0 -13 Td
/F1 8 Tf
( ) Tj
0 -12 Td
/F2 10 Tf
(Keywords: Luira Phanit, Chithar, Awungshi, Hao Pheichak, Agrarian Liturgy, Ruivah, Manipur) Tj
0 -14 Td
ET
