(1. CULTURAL SIGNIFICANCE & CHRONOLOGY OF LUIRA) Tj
0 -16 Td
/F1 8 Tf
( ) Tj
0 -12 Td
/F1 9 Tf
(Luira Phanit marks the dawn of the agricultural calendar. Before any) Tj
0 -13 Td
/F1 9 Tf
(villager may sow seed in their terraced fields, the village priest and) Tj
0 -13 Td
/F1 9 Tf
(chief \(Awungshi\) must perform the sacred ritual of Chithar \(first seed) Tj
0 -13 Td
/F1 9 Tf
(offering\) to conciliate Ameo \(the benevolent earth guardian deity\). The) Tj
0 -13 Td
/F1 9 Tf
(festival extends across seven ceremonial days: Luishat \(preparation\),) Tj
0 -13 Td
/F1 9 Tf
(Phanit-khara \(arrival\), Pheichak \(communal dance\), and Ngashan \(clan) Tj
0 -13 Td
/F1 9 Tf
(feasting\).) Tj
0 -13 Td
/F1 8 Tf
( ) Tj
0 -12 Td
/F2 10 Tf
(Tangkhul Linguistic Data & Analysis:) Tj
0 -14 Td
/F2 9 Tf
(  * Luira Phanit : Seed sowing festival) Tj
0 -13 Td
/F1 8 Tf
(    Analysis: lui \(field\) + ra \(seed/root\) + phanit \(sacred feast\).) Tj
0 -12 Td
/F2 9 Tf
(  * Chithar : first sacred seed sowing ritual) Tj
0 -13 Td
/F1 8 Tf
(    Analysis: Chi \(paddy seed\) + thar \(consecration/first blessing\).) Tj
0 -12 Td
/F2 9 Tf
(  * Awungshi : hereditary village chief and high priest) Tj
0 -13 Td
/F1 8 Tf
(    Analysis: Custodian of village agrarian rituals.) Tj
