(2. SACRED INVOCATIONAL LITURGY: THE CHITHAR PRAYER) Tj
0 -16 Td
/F1 8 Tf
( ) Tj
0 -12 Td
/F1 9 Tf
(At dawn on the third day, the Awungshi enters the ancestral sacred plot) Tj
0 -13 Td
/F1 9 Tf
(\(Awung-luiram\) accompanied by clan elders. Scattering seven handfuls of) Tj
0 -13 Td
/F1 9 Tf
(consecrated paddy seeds onto the newly turned earth, he chants the) Tj
0 -13 Td
/F1 9 Tf
(ancient invocation pleading for abundant rain, pest protection, and) Tj
0 -13 Td
/F1 9 Tf
(communal bumper harvests.) Tj
0 -13 Td
/F1 8 Tf
( ) Tj
0 -12 Td
/F2 10 Tf
(Tangkhul Linguistic Data & Analysis:) Tj
0 -14 Td
/F2 9 Tf
(  * 'Kazingkhamang eina rarlu, Kazingramwui tui-ngapom hung-kachamlaga ngaleili hung-sungsaklu!' : O celestial rains come forth, let heaven's moisture descend upon the soil!) Tj
0 -13 Td
/F1 8 Tf
(    Analysis: Archaic meteorological invocation.) Tj
0 -12 Td
/F2 9 Tf
(  * 'Hao naorapli kasham makasalu, theiwon kapha khangaraorap eina kashungsaklu!' : Spare the children of Hao from famine, fill their granaries with joyful abundance!) Tj
0 -13 Td
/F1 8 Tf
(    Analysis: Community protection formula.) Tj
0 -12 Td
